				<div id="ai-features">
					<h2 class="font-display text-xl font-medium text-primary">9. AI Features</h2>
					<p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
						We use artificial intelligence to generate suggested captions, profile summaries, and place
						categorizations, and to rank recommendations.
					</p>
					<h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-semibold text-primary">What is sent to AI providers</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
						Depending on the feature: labels derived from your photos, names of cities you have visited,
						place names and categories, and — for photo categorization and caption suggestions —
						<strong>the photo images themselves</strong>.
					</p>
					<h3 class="mt-5 text-base font-semibold text-primary">Providers</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">Google Vertex AI (Gemini models) and Google Cloud Vision.</p>
					<h3 class="mt-5 text-base font-semibold text-primary">Isolation</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
						Prompts contain only your own information. We do not include other users' content in
						requests made on your behalf.
					</p>
					<p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
						<strong>Your profile summary and taste profile are visible only to you</strong> and are not
						displayed to other users.
					</p>
					<h3 class="mt-5 text-base font-semibold text-primary">Retention and training by providers</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
						We do not train models on user information or photos provided. This is enforced by Google.
					</p>
					<h3 class="mt-5 text-base font-semibold text-primary">Accuracy</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
						AI output may be wrong. You review and can edit generated content before it is published.
					</p>
					<p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
						<strong>We do not make automated decisions producing legal or similarly significant effects
						about you.</strong>
					</p>
				</div>

				<div id="how-we-share-information">
					<h2 class="font-display text-xl font-medium text-primary">10. How We Share Information</h2>

					<h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-semibold text-primary">10.1 With other users</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
						When you post an experience, you choose who can see it:
					</p>
					<ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
						<li><strong>Public</strong> — visible to any other Log user.</li>
						<li><strong>Friends</strong> — visible only to accounts that follow you, and to yourself.</li>
						<li><strong>Private</strong> — visible only to you.</li>
					</ul>
					<p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
						This is enforced by our database's own access-control rules — the restriction holds no
						matter how the content is requested, not only within the app's normal screens. This applies
						to the post itself and to its photos: photo files are access-controlled the same way, not
						separately public.
					</p>
					<p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
						<strong>Blocking.</strong> If you block another user, neither of you can see the other's
						posts or photos, in either direction, regardless of that content's visibility setting. This
						is enforced at the same database level, not only hidden from view in the app.
					</p>
					<p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
						<strong>Your profile.</strong> Other users can see your name, username, profile photo, bio,
						and current city. They cannot see your email address, phone number, or date of birth. The
						one exception: if another user is a confirmed friend, we may surface that your birthday is
						coming up — that access is limited to actual friends and to that purpose.
					</p>
					<p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
						Likes, comments, and follows on a post are visible to other users of the app.
					</p>

					<h3 class="mt-5 text-base font-semibold text-primary">10.2 With service providers</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-text/80">
						We share information with vendors who process it on our behalf, under contract, for the
						purposes below.
					</p>
					<div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
						<table class="w-full min-w-[640px] border-collapse text-sm">
							<thead>
								<tr class="border-b hairline text-left">
